them:1. Achieving Net-Zero GoalsBusinesses are under pressure to commit to net-zero emissions. Carbon credits help offset emissions that cannot be eliminated immediately.2. Enhancing Brand ImageConsumers are increasingly eco-conscious. Companies using carbon credits can market themselves as sustainable and responsible, gaining trust and loyalty.3. Financial OpportunitiesCarbon credits are tradable assets. Businesses can:Earn revenue by selling excess creditsReduce costs by optimizing emissions4. Compliance with RegulationsIndia is strengthening its climate policies. Companies that fail to comply may face penalties. Carbon credits ensure businesses stay within legal limits.5. Attracting InvestorsInvestors now consider ESG (Environmental, Social, Governance) factors. Companies actively managing carbon emissions are more attractive for funding and partnerships using ESG Advisory.#pro-gallery-c7bp429316-not-scoped .gallery-item-container { opacity: 0 }
